<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Coverage collection for `dotnet test` (coverlet.collector, already referenced by the test
  project). build.ps1 passes this file and reads the root line-rate of the Cobertura report
  it produces under publish/coverage; -CoverageFloor turns the number into a gate.

  Exclusions, and why:
  - NeonSidekick.Audio.WinMm*: the WinMM device classes (playback, capture, the imports) run
    only against a real device and only prove anything in the PUBLISHED binary (the NAudio
    by-value-marshalling scar was invisible under the JIT). They are gated by the published-exe
    smoke (audio:winmm, audio:winmm-in) and by the audio and voice checks on the published exe,
    not by line coverage. (No double hyphen in this comment: XML forbids it, and dotnet test
    rejects the whole file.)
  - NeonSidekick.Viewer.PictureWindow* and ViewerNative (2026-09-27): the picture viewer's Win32 window, its thread
    and imports; a window, a message loop and a folder watcher prove themselves by hand and by the published-exe smoke
    (viewer:window; viewer:drag for PictureWindowDrag, 2026-09-28, the shell's data object behind the drag out). ViewerState
    and ViewerImage, where its decisions and its decode live, stay covered. NeonSidekick.Viewer.LogWindow* and WindowChrome
    (2026-10-02): the log window's Win32 window and thread, and the frame it shares with the picture viewer (full screen, the
    place it last closed, the themed bar), proven by hand and by the smoke (viewer:log-window). LogViewState, LogViewStyle and
    LogViewText, where its decisions live, stay covered. NeonSidekick.Viewer.ThumbsWindow* and ContextMenuWindow (2026-10-04):
    the thumbnail browser's Win32 window, its thread, watcher and reads, and the picture menu's popups; proven by hand and by the
    smoke (viewer:thumbs, viewer:menu). ThumbsState, ThumbCache, ContextMenuState, MenuStyle, PictureMenu and PictureActions, where
    their decisions live, stay covered. NeonSidekick.Viewer.WebViewNative and WebViewHost (2026-10-05): the video window's WebView2
    vtable calls and the chain over them; they need the WebView2 Runtime and a window's message loop, and prove themselves in the
    published-exe smoke (video:webview2, also run under the JIT by WebViewTests). VideoPage and WebViewHandler, the page and the
    app-made COM objects, stay covered. NeonSidekick.Viewer.VideoWindow* (2026-10-05): the video window and its thread, proven by hand on the
    published exe; VideoMessages, VideoKeys, VideoText and the VideoPlayer records, where its decisions live, stay covered.
    NeonSidekick.Viewer.BrowserWindow* (2026-10-13): the Browser window and its thread, proven by browser:webview2 (the new slots)
    and by hand; BrowserPage, BrowserWatch, BrowserKeys, BrowserAnswers and BrowserText, where its decisions live, stay covered
    (BrowserFullScreen too, 2026-10-14: F11's full screen and the page's own).
    BrowserBarNative (later that day): its navigation bar's EDIT, focus and comctl32 tooltip calls, proven by the same probe
    (the box and a tooltip made); BrowserToolbar and BrowserAddress, the bar's layout, state and addresses, stay covered.
  - NeonSidekick.Printing.WindowsPrintSpooler* and PrintNative (2026-09-28): the printers, a printer's device context and the
    shell's print verb; they need a real spooler and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (print:spooler, a job to
    Microsoft Print to PDF) and a live fact. PrintLayout, PrintService and PrintCommand, where the decisions live, stay covered.
    Their Mac twins MacPrintSpooler, MacPdfDocument, MacPdfNative and CupsNative (2026-10-08, printing on a Mac): libcups'
    destinations, paper and jobs, and CoreGraphics' PDF context with CoreText; they need a Mac (and, to submit, a queue) and
    prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (print:cups), the Mac facts that read the PDFs back and a held-and-cancelled
    live fact. MacPrintRules, where the paper, faces, coordinates and options live, stays covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Perf.PerfNative, WindowsPerfSource, NvmlGpu and PdhGpu (2026-09-29): the performance bar's kernel32, NVML,
    DXGI and PDH readers; they read the real machine and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (perf:kernel32,
    perf:nvml, perf:pdh-dxgi). PerfMath, PerfSampler and PerfBar, where the arithmetic and the drawing live, stay covered.
    Their Mac twins MacPerfNative, MacPerfSource, MacGpu and MacNetworkCounters (2026-10-07): Mach, sysctl, IOKit and
    CoreFoundation on the real machine, proven by the published-exe smoke there (perf:mach, perf:iokit, perf:network); the tick,
    page and ifmibdata arithmetic is PerfMath's and stays covered.
  - NeonSidekick.Camera.CameraNative and MediaFoundationCameraSystem (2026-10-02): the camera's Media Foundation vtable calls
    and the reader over them; they need Windows' media stack and, past the list, a real camera, and prove themselves in the
    published-exe smoke (camera:mf, the slots that need no camera) and by camera-check on a real one, plus the live facts.
    CameraSession, CameraFormats, CameraPixels, CameraJpeg, FrameDiff and CameraWatch, where the decisions live, stay covered.
    Their Mac twins MacCameraNative and MacCameraSystem (2026-10-07): AVFoundation, CoreMedia, CoreVideo and libdispatch, the
    delegate class made at runtime and the permission's block; they need a Mac and, past the list, a camera and the terminal's
    permission, and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke there (camera:avf) and by camera-check, plus the live facts.
    MacCameraRules, where the format, rate, warm-up, permission and error decisions live, stays covered on every OS; so does
    MacLiveWindow's twin on Windows' side, LiveView. MacLiveWindow* rides with the AppKit windows below.
  - NeonSidekick.UI.UnixConsoleInput and TermiosNative (2026-10-06, the macOS build): the terminal reader over libc's termios,
    poll and read; they run only on macOS against a real terminal and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke there
    (console:termios). VtInputParser, where every byte rule lives, stays covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Shell.GroupChild and PosixSpawnNative (2026-10-12, the Mac's orphans): the shell runner's posix_spawnp, waitid
    and killpg; they run only on macOS (the Unix runner tests drive them there) and prove themselves in the smoke (shell:posix-spawn).
    PosixExit, the exit-code rule, stays covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Sql.MacKeychain and KeychainNative (2026-10-06, the macOS build): the Keychain behind the secrets on macOS;
    they need a Mac's login Keychain and prove themselves in the smoke there (keys:keychain).
  - NeonSidekick.UI.MacClipboard (2026-10-06): pbcopy/pbpaste, which exist only on macOS.
  - NeonSidekick.Images.ImageIONative and ImageIOCodecs (2026-10-07, pictures on a Mac): ImageIO, CoreGraphics, CoreFoundation and
    vImage behind MagicScaler, and the decoder and encoder over them; they run only on macOS and prove themselves in the smoke there
    (image:imageio, image:resize, image:edit, splash:decode, camera:encode) and in the Mac test run. ImageIOFormats, where the format
    table, the magic bytes, the option and metadata mapping and the pixel shuffles live, stays covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Audio.AudioQueuePlayback, AudioQueueCapture and AudioQueueNative (2026-10-07, sound on a Mac): the
    AudioQueue pair, Core Audio's default devices and the microphone permission's Objective-C message; they run only on
    macOS against real devices (and a terminal's permission) and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke there
    (audio:audioqueue, audio:audioqueue-in), in audio-check and voice-check, and in the device facts. PlaybackLedger,
    SilenceWatch, MicrophoneAccess, MicrophoneText and AudioQueueText, where the byte accounting, the silence verdict and the
    wording live, stay covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Viewer.AppKit* (AppKitNative, AppKitHost, AppKitClasses, AppKitWindow), MainTimer, MacKeyEvent and
    MacPictureWindow*, MacThumbsWindow*, MacLineWindow*, MacLiveWindow*, MacPictureMenu and MacTerminal (2026-10-07, the app's own windows over AppKit on a Mac): the Objective-C runtime, the main-thread host,
    the classes made at runtime and the windows over them; AppKit runs only on a process's main thread, which xUnit's testhost
    never gives a test, so they prove themselves in the published-exe smoke there (viewer:window) and by hand. MacKeys,
    MacPlacement and TerminalPick, where the key map, the places' arithmetic and the terminal's choice live, stay covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Screen.MacScreenNative and MacScreenSystem (2026-10-07, screen capture on a Mac): CoreGraphics' display and
    window lists, the Screen Recording permission, and ScreenCaptureKit's screenshots through hand-built completion blocks; they
    need a window server and the terminal's permission, and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (screen:cg, screen:sck)
    and by hand. MacScreenRules, where the shared space, the window rules, the terminal's own window and the canvas plan live,
    and ScreenCapture's refusal and listing, stay covered on every OS.
  - NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacWebKit and MacVideoWindow* (2026-10-07, YouTube playback on a Mac): WebKit, the web view's delegate
    class made at runtime, the navigation decision's block, and the video window over them on the AppKit host; they need a
    process's main thread and a window server, and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (video:webkit) and the live run.
    WebKitPage, where the bridge, the frame rule and the data store's identifier live, and MacKeys' video keys stay covered.
  - NeonSidekick.Shortcuts.MacShortcutWriter (2026-10-08, /shortcut on a Mac): NSWorkspace's icon and per-file Open-with
    binding; they change a real file's Finder state and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (shortcut:command) and by
    hand. DesktopShortcut, where the name, the command line, the zsh quoting and the script's text live, and TerminalPick, stay covered.
  - NeonSidekick.Unc.MacMountSystem and NetFSNative (2026-10-11, UNC shares on a Mac): NetFS's mount, getfsstat and unmount;
    they mount real shares, so they prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (unc:netfs, which never mounts), the unc-check mode
    and the live facts against a loopback share. ShareMounts and MacMountRules, where the keys, the reuse, the records, the
    sweep and the refusals live, stay covered on every OS over FakeMountSystem.
  - NeonSidekick.Hotkeys.MacHotkeyNative and MacHotkeyProbe (2026-10-11, /keycheck on a Mac): HIToolbox's symbolic hotkeys and
    exclusive register, and the terminals' preferences through cfprefsd; they need a window server and ask the live system, so
    they prove themselves in the published-exe smoke (keys:carbon), a Mac fact and by hand. MacHotkeyRules, where the key codes,
    the fn rule, the order of the checks and the Option settings' readings live, stays covered on every OS.
  - Program: the composition root; the smoke run on the published exe covers it.
  - NeonSidekick.EventLog.WindowsEventLogSystem and EventLogNative (2026-10-15, the event logs): wevtapi.dll over this PC's own
    logs, proven by the smoke's eventlog:wevtapi, eventlog:rpc-login and eventlog:evtx on the published binary and by
    EventLogWindowsTests on Windows; a Mac has no event logs. The policy over any reader (EventLogSearch, the XPath, the XML,
    the variants, the redaction) stays covered on every OS.
  - The admin families' native layers (2026-10-15, the admin-tools plan): NeonSidekick.Network.WindowsPinger and IcmpSocketPinger
    (iphlpapi's echo and a datagram ICMP socket, the real network), NeonSidekick.Services.ServiceNative and WindowsServiceSystem
    (advapi32's Service Control Manager), NeonSidekick.Tasks.TaskNative and WindowsTaskSystem (the Task Scheduler's COM vtables),
    NeonSidekick.ActiveDirectory.LdapNative, WindowsDirectorySystem and DomainJoinNative (wldap32 and netapi32). They need this
    machine's services, scheduler, a domain controller or a raw socket, and prove themselves in the published-exe smoke
    (net:icmp, services:scm, services:remote, tasks:com, tasks:remote, ad:wldap32), the Windows facts and the live facts against
    the samba_ad_dev container. Everything over them (the wire formats, the order of checks, the renderers, the queries) stays
    covered on every OS against the fakes.
  - GeneratedCodeAttribute / ExcludeFromCodeCoverageAttribute: source-generated JSON contexts,
    LibraryImport stubs and GeneratedRegex bodies. CompilerGeneratedAttribute is deliberately
    NOT excluded: that would drop every async state machine and lambda body.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <DataCollectionRunSettings>
    <DataCollectors>
      <DataCollector friendlyName="XPlat Code Coverage">
        <Configuration>
          <Format>cobertura</Format>
          <Exclude>[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Audio.WinMm*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Audio.AudioQueuePlayback,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Audio.AudioQueueCapture,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Audio.AudioQueueNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.PictureWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.ViewerNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.LogWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.WindowChrome*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.ThumbsWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.ContextMenuWindow,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.WebViewNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.WebViewHost*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.VideoWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.BrowserWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.BrowserBarNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Printing.WindowsPrintSpooler*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Printing.PrintNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Printing.MacPrintSpooler,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Printing.MacPdfDocument,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Printing.MacPdfNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Printing.CupsNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.PerfNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.WindowsPerfSource,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.NvmlGpu,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.PdhGpu,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.MacPerfNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.MacPerfSource,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.MacGpu,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Perf.MacNetworkCounters,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Camera.CameraNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Camera.MediaFoundationCameraSystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Camera.MacCameraNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Camera.MacCameraSystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.UI.UnixConsoleInput,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.UI.TermiosNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Shell.PosixSpawnNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Shell.GroupChild,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Sql.MacKeychain,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Sql.KeychainNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.UI.MacClipboard,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Images.ImageIONative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Images.ImageIOCodecs*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.AppKit*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MainTimer,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacKeyEvent,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacPictureWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacThumbsWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacPictureMenu,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacLineWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacLiveWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacTerminal,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacWebKit,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Viewer.MacVideoWindow*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Screen.MacScreenNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Screen.MacScreenSystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Shortcuts.MacShortcutWriter,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Unc.MacMountSystem,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Unc.NetFSNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Hotkeys.MacHotkeyNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Hotkeys.MacHotkeyProbe,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.EventLog.WindowsEventLogSystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.EventLog.EventLogNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Network.WindowsPinger,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Network.IcmpSocketPinger,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Services.ServiceNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Services.WindowsServiceSystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Tasks.TaskNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.Tasks.WindowsTaskSystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.ActiveDirectory.LdapNative,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.ActiveDirectory.WindowsDirectorySystem*,[NeonSidekick]NeonSidekick.ActiveDirectory.DomainJoinNative,[NeonSidekick]Program</Exclude>
          <ExcludeByAttribute>GeneratedCodeAttribute,ExcludeFromCodeCoverageAttribute</ExcludeByAttribute>
          <SkipAutoProps>true</SkipAutoProps>
          <IncludeTestAssembly>false</IncludeTestAssembly>
        </Configuration>
      </DataCollector>
    </DataCollectors>
  </DataCollectionRunSettings>
</RunSettings>
